    "body": "This is a demonstration of a twelve-week postpartum follow-through service. Every patient, name, and number on screen is made up. What it is: short check-ins, a plain-language care plan, and a named contact. It also has a practice queue where a person owns each item until an outcome is logged. What it is not: it is not emergency care. It is not a substitute for your care team. It is not therapy. No program reads or answers what a patient writes. Nothing here has been assessed by a regulator. Practice phone numbers are placeholders. The crisis line (988) and 911 are real.",
